evals.prompt:
Write a Go native fuzz test (using testing.F, Go 1.18+ style) for this function:

```go
func ParseDuration(s string) (time.Duration, error) {
    return time.ParseDuration(s)
}
```

Seed it with at least two real example inputs, and assert a property that should hold for any input that parses successfully (for example, that formatting the parsed duration back and reparsing it produces the same value), rather than a fixed table of expected outputs.
